.TP
.B qargi agent
Name the members: the local agents that do the work.
.PP
A member is a Claude Code subagent you name, rendered from the one member definition qargi ships, with the abilities it serves: build, write, review, test (all four by default). Each ability is a skill (qargi\-build, qargi\-write, qargi\-review, qargi\-test) the member loads when the task block names it. Review is read\-only as a rule: the guard refuses changes to the clone under that ability. Under every ability it refuses the verbs that change a skill (qargi skill|tool new, import, seal, remove, link, unlink, enable, disable; qargi discover install; qargi packs apply) and writes in the pack library, the credentials directory and install.json, ~/.claude/skills and any .claude/skills directory; it fails closed. Dispatch spawns the member qargi agent for ABILITY prints.
